  {
   "id": 233281,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<p><img src=\"exercises/media/cc475f0b4d0117ad.jpg\" alt=\"The figure shows a normal gene with segments 1 through 4, a 5' UTR, and a 3'UTR. This gene has ++ expression. Below, deletion 1 is in the 5' UTR. This mutant has +++ expression. Below that, deletion 2 is in the very 5' end of the 5' UTR. This mutant has ++ expression. Below that, deletion 3 is in segment 2. This mutant has + expression. Below that, deletion 4 is in the 3' UTR. This mutant has ++ expression\"></p>\n\n<p>The level of transcription of a gene is tested by creating deletions in the gene as shown in the illustration. These modified genes are tested for their level of transcription: (++) normal transcription levels; (+) low transcription levels; (+++) high transcription levels. Which deletion is in an enhancer involved in regulating the gene?</p>\n",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 723267,
     "content_html": "deletion 1"
    },
    {
     "id": 723268,
     "content_html": "deletion 2"
    },
    {
     "id": 723270,
     "content_html": "deletion 3"
    },
    {
     "id": 723269,
     "content_html": "deletion 4"
    }
   ],
